  "verbalization": "Zedoalactone C appears to interact with DNA polymerase iota through a multi-step pathway, where it first targets Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which in turn is a target of Kandenol D. This suggests a potential mechanism involving the modulation of phosphatase activity, which could influence the function of DNA polymerase iota. The evidence from both paths indicates that Zedoalactone C may act as a modulator of the signaling cascade leading to DNA polymerase iota activation. The presence of a direct target relationship between Zedoalactone C and DNA polymerase iota, as well as the indirect pathway through Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, supports the idea that Zedoalactone C may influence DNA polymerase iota activity through a complex regulatory network. The integration of these findings highlights the importance of phosphatase activity in the regulation of DNA polymerase iota, suggesting a possible role for Zedoalactone C in modulating this process.",
